## 10. Leakage demonstration

{{ leakage | table }}

A random split puts transactions from the same account on both sides, so the model can recognise accounts it has already seen labelled. The time split is the honest estimate of performance on future transactions.

## 11. Limitations and next steps

- Many columns are anonymised, so some reasons are hard to act on, and their point-in-time safety cannot be verified.
- There is no investigator feedback or online learning.
- Fraud labels spread across an account's later transactions in this data, which flatters repeat detection.
- Online alerts use a fixed threshold, so they can differ from the ranked daily queue.
- Next: monitor score PSI, precision on reviewed alerts and capacity breaches; retrain on a schedule; add feedback labels.
